column7:
Open data can provide important information on the state of the housing market and homelessness. The ministry for social affairs conducted a study to evaluate the data basis for homelessness to increase evidence-based policy-making: https://www.oeaw.ac.at/isr/wohnen-und-urbane-oekonomie/datenbasis-obdachlosigkeit-wohnungslosigkeit;
Open government data on building type data (year built) and listed protected buidlings are used for a rent-calculation, e. g. https://wiener-mietenrechner.at/; 
Statistik Austria provides data on the whole housing market / census data, including e.g. data on housing problems in different legal relationsships (rent, owner, public housing, etc.), https://statcube.at/statistik.at/ext/statcube/jsf/tableView/tableView.xhtml, or housing costs: https://www.statistik.at/statistiken/bevoelkerung-und-soziales/wohnen/wohnkosten
